"""Canine chocolate calculator; clinical source facts stay explicit in the page/model."""
from pathlib import Path
import re,runpy
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];D=R/'dist'
prefix=(D/'drugs.html').read_text().split('<main id="main-content"')[0]
prefix=prefix.replace('Drugs · ER Reference','Chocolate Toxicity · ER Reference').replace('data-tool="drugs"','data-tool="chocolate"').replace('class="potassium-page"','class="potassium-page chocolate-page"').replace('— Drugs','— Chocolate Toxicity')
prefix=re.sub(r' aria-current="page"','',prefix);prefix=prefix.replace('<span class="current-page">Current</span>','')
icons={
'below':'<path d="M9 18 6 7l10 5h16l10-5-3 11v13c0 9-8 13-15 13S9 40 9 31Z"/><path d="M17 25h1m12 0h1m-12 9q5 5 10 0"/><path d="m22 29 2 2 2-2Z"/>',
'gi':'<path d="M20 5v12c0 5-9 3-11 10-3 10 5 17 14 17 13 0 20-9 17-21-2-8-10-13-12-6-2 5-7 4-7-1V5"/><path d="m28 28 5-2m-13 8 6 3"/>',
'cardiac':'<path d="M24 42 6 25C-5 11 13 1 24 14 35 1 53 11 42 25Z"/><path d="M5 25h11l4-9 6 18 4-9h13"/>',
'neuro':'<path d="M24 8c-6-8-16-1-14 6-8 1-9 12-3 16-3 10 9 17 17 10 8 7 20 0 17-10 6-4 5-15-3-16 2-7-8-14-14-6Z"/><path d="M24 8v32m-14-26 7 6-4 6m20-12-5 7 6 7m-20 6 6-4m11 6-5-5"/>',
'lethal':'<path d="M10 30C-5 6 12 2 24 2s29 4 14 28l-5 3v11H15V33Z"/><circle cx="16" cy="21" r="4"/><circle cx="32" cy="21" r="4"/><path d="m24 27-3 5h6Zm-4 10v7m8-7v7"/>'}
def icon(key):return f'<svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" width="38" height="38" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">{icons[key]}</svg>'
bands=[('below','Below reference','&lt;20 mg/kg','Not a “normal” or safe guarantee.'),('gi','GI upset','~20 mg/kg','Vomiting, diarrhea, thirst may occur.'),('cardiac','Cardiac','40–50 mg/kg','Cardiac effects. Call animal poison control.'),('neuro','Neurologic','≥60 mg/kg','Seizure risk. Call animal poison control.'),('lethal','Severe toxicity / LD₅₀','LD₅₀: 100–200 mg/kg','Not a death threshold; deaths can occur below this range. Call animal poison control.')]
body='''<main id="main-content" class="chocolate-main"><div class="eyebrow">TOXICOLOGY / DOGS</div><h1>Chocolate toxicity</h1><div hidden><input id="weight" type="number"><select id="species"><option value=""></option><option>Dog</option><option>Cat</option></select></div><p class="help">Uses the shared patient above. Blank patient fields default to Dog / 20 kg; a blank single amount defaults to 1 oz. <a href="#chocolate-sources">Merck source & calculation notes</a>.</p>
<div class="chocolate-layout"><section class="panel"><h2>What was eaten?</h2><div id="chocEntries"></div><div class="chocolate-actions"><button type="button" id="chocAdd">+ Add another product</button><button type="button" id="chocClear">Clear chocolate entries</button><small id="chocEntryCount"></small></div><p class="help">Use chocolate-component weight for mixed foods, not the entire brownie/cookie. For high-cocoa bars, choose the cocoa-% option instead of generic sweet dark.</p></section><section class="panel chocolate-results" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"><h2>Estimated exposure</h2><div class="chocolate-dose-display"><span id="chocDoseIcon" hidden aria-hidden="true"></span><strong id="chocDose">—</strong></div><p id="chocDefaults" class="chocolate-defaults"></p><p id="chocRiskLabel" class="chocolate-risk-label"></p><p id="chocPoisonRecommendation" class="chocolate-poison-recommendation" hidden>Recommendation: Call animal poison control.</p><p id="chocWhiteConcern" class="chocolate-white-concern" hidden><strong>White chocolate: high-fat / GI concerns</strong><br>Low methylxanthine exposure does not rule out GI upset. Consider pancreatitis in susceptible patients based on the amount eaten, history and clinical signs. <a href="#chocolate-sources">Merck source</a>.</p><p id="chocTotal">—</p><p id="chocStatus">Select Dog, weight, source and amount.</p><p class="help">Total methylxanthines = theobromine + caffeine. Treat clinical signs and the exposure history; this estimate does not predict an individual outcome.</p></section></div>
<section id="chocComparison" class="panel table-wrap" aria-live="polite" hidden></section>
<section class="panel chocolate-band-panel"><h2>Canine dose references</h2><div class="chocolate-band-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Connected canine dose reference bands"><div class="chocolate-band-track"><div class="chocolate-boundaries" aria-hidden="true"><span>0</span><span>20</span><span>40</span><span>60</span><span>100</span><span>200 mg/kg</span></div><div class="chocolate-risk-line" aria-hidden="true"></div><span id="chocRiskDot" class="chocolate-risk-dot" hidden aria-hidden="true"></span><div class="chocolate-bands">'''
body+=''.join(f'<article class="chocolate-band" data-choc-band="{key}" data-active="false">{icon(key)}<h3>{title}</h3><b>{dose}</b><p>{note}</p><small class="band-match"></small></article>' for key,title,dose,note in bands)
body+='''</div></div></div><p id="chocPosition" class="help chocolate-position">Enter an exposure to place the dose marker.</p><p id="chocQuickMath" class="chocolate-quick-math"></p><p class="help">The dot follows the upper estimate between reference boundaries. Bands have equal widths, not a linear mg/kg scale; values above 200 mg/kg stay at the far end. These are overlapping risk references, not a mandatory progression. The upper estimate is highlighted; the lethal category uses the lower end of the reported LD₅₀ range for attention, not a prediction of death.</p></section>
<section class="panel chocolate-clinical"><h2>Clinical quick reference</h2><div class="clinical-mini-grid"><div><h3>Decontamination</h3><p>Clinically normal, recent ingestion (eg, within 2 hr): consider emesis. Stabilize symptomatic patients first.</p></div><div><h3>Activated charcoal</h3><p>Merck limits consideration to lethal exposures after weighing dehydration and hypernatremia risks.</p></div><div><h3>Monitoring / support</h3><p>ECG, temperature, electrolytes and fluid support; manage arrhythmias and CNS signs. Onset may be delayed 6–12 hr.</p></div></div><p class="help">No automatic treatment or medication doses are generated. White chocolate’s low methylxanthines do not address fat-related illness or other ingredients; assess co-ingestants separately.</p></section>
<details class="panel"><summary>Exposure math</summary><pre id="chocMath"></pre></details>
<details class="panel" id="chocolate-sources"><summary>Sources & assumptions</summary><p><a href="https://www.merckvetmanual.com/toxicology/food-hazards/chocolate-toxicosis-in-animals">Merck Veterinary Manual · Chocolate Toxicosis in Animals</a> — updated February 2026; reviewed October 17, 2026. Concentrations and canine dose references come from this page.</p><p>Calculation: chocolate grams × total methylxanthines (mg/g) ÷ patient kg. Semisweet/sweet dark retains the 5.3–5.6 mg/g range; other listed types use Merck’s approximate values. Cocoa-% estimate = 15.5 mg/g × cocoa fraction, an approximation rather than a brand assay. Brands and recipes vary.</p><p>Mass units: 1 avoirdupois oz = 28.349523125 g. Both input units use the same mg/g model, so converting units preserves exposure. Merck’s separately rounded mg/oz table may therefore differ slightly. All entered products are added; a partly completed entry prevents a complete estimate. This models ingested amount without subtracting emesis or estimating absorbed dose.</p><p id="chocolate-portion-source"><a href="https://www.verybestbaking.com/toll-house/products/semi-sweet-chocolate-morsels-12oz/">NESTLÉ Toll House semi-sweet morsels label</a>: 1 Tbsp = 14 g. Derived rough portions: 2 Tbsp (⅛ US cup) ≈ 28 g ≈ 1 oz; ¼ US cup ≈ 56 g ≈ 2 oz. Chip size and packing vary. Bar-square weights vary by product; use package mass divided by equal pieces. This source supports portion estimates only; methylxanthine values and risk references remain Merck-based.</p><p>Cocoa hull methylxanthines may vary with processing. Unknown products, recipes and co-ingestants need product-specific assessment. Canine risk interpretation is disabled for cats. Illustrations are symbolic labels, not clinical photographs.</p></details><footer>Veterinary reference draft · Calculation checks do not replace independent clinical validation. <a href="sources.html#chocolate-source">Source record</a>.</footer></main><script src="chocolate-calc.js"></script><script src="chocolate.js"></script><script src="navigation.js"></script><script src="patient-context.js"></script></body></html>'''
(D/'chocolate.html').write_text(prefix+body)
runpy.run_path(str(R/'scripts/finalize-site.py'))
